 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to the taking of deer in the county of Suffolk",
    "basePrintNo": "S4666",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4666-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0907, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4666\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to the taking of deer in the county of Suffolk\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the time period for the taking the deer by long bow in the\nCounty of Suffolk from December 31st until March 31st.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends Item (h) of paragraph a of subdivision 2 of Section 11-0907 of\nthe Environmental Conservation Law to extend the time period for the\ntaking the deer by long bow in the County of Suffolk from December\n31st until March 31st.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current long bow season for taking deer in Suffolk County, as\nregulated by the New York State Department of Environmental\nConservation, is from October 1st through December 31st. With the\nrecent explosion of Suffolk County's deer population, communities and\nmunicipalities are looking for ways to expand hunting opportunities to\nhelp control the deer population. The excessive deer population on\neastern Long Island poses a threat to public health, public safety,\npersonal property, and the environment. Allowing for the expansion of\nthe long bow season for deer in Suffolk County for an additional three\nmonths, through the end of March, can further help reduce the size of\nthe herd.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2014: A.9017/S.6767\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, the\namendments to item (h) of paragraph a of subdivision 2 of Section\n11-0907 of the Environmental Conservation Law made by Section 1 of\nthis act shall be subject to the expiration and reversion of such\nparagraph pursuant to Section 13 of Chapter 600 of the Laws of 1993,\nwhen upon such date the provisions of Section 2 of this act shall take\neffect.\n\n",
